    "created_at": "2017-04-17T14:35:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-17T14:35:09Z",
    "body": "So technically clearing the pointer back has no normative effect, but it's probably a good idea to document that so that implementations which are sticking close to the spec's structure have an easier time.\r\n\r\nSo, action items:\r\n\r\n- Clear the pointer back in step 7.1 as noted\r\n- Add a note to ParseScript/ParseModule calls pointing out that their last parameter sets [[HostDefined]].",
